  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit and maximum uncertainty across all design axes (modality, profile strategy, encoder choice, aggregation, fusion). The most critical first question is: what is the baseline performance of the simplest, most standard configuration? config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the canonical starting point in single-cell RNA-seq profiling—it uses the most common dimensionality reduction (PCA to 2000 dims), avoids any learned encoder or aggregation complexity, and isolates the RNA signal. Establishing this baseline is a prerequisite for interpreting every subsequent experiment: without it, we cannot tell whether multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation, or learned encoders actually add value. It is the highest-information first experiment because it anchors the entire search space and reduces the most uncertainty per experiment run."
}

